Wednesday Update
-- Trade Alert: No new recommendations amid chop and low volume-- Stocks mo=
destly higher as investors re-rate Alphabet higher*Stocks were spinning sid=
eways with an upward bias in midday trade on Wednesday, with Alphabet (GOOG=
) outshining Amazon (AMZN) following Jeff Bezos leaving CEO role later in t=
he year amid their strong quarterly results.Through 2:45 pm the major index=
es were up around 3%. At current levels, the Dow and the S&amp;P are sittin=
g close to the record levels struck late last month on bets of an economic =
revival aided by heavy stimulus packages.Alphabet climbed to a record high =
and was up 8% after a strong recovery in advertising revenue lifted its Q4 =
performance. The strong showing triggered a slew of price target upgrades a=
mong analysts, sending the stock crossing the $2,000 mark."It is relatively=
 rare that we see compelling reasons for mega-cap stocks to re-rate higher =
but this is one of those times," said Michael Levine, an analyst at Pivotal=
 Research.Amazon recovered to rise 0.7% after faltering earlier as Amazon W=
eb Services head Andy Jassy is set to replace Bezos in Q3. "This confirms t=
hat AMZN does not plan to spin off AWS, unless forced to by regulatory fact=
ors," Oppenheimer analyst Jason Helfstein said in a note.Meanwhile, Amgen (=
AMGN) sank more than 3% as focus shifted to its growth prospects following =
its Q4 results. "While Amgen is good at managing the P&amp;L, we are starti=
ng to have growth concerns over the coming years -- while it is not enough =
to justify a formal downgrade, it is something we're closely watching," sai=
d Credit Suisse analysts in a note.On the energy front, oil prices rose, wi=
th US West Texas Intermediate up 2.3% to $56.02 per barrel and Brent crude =
2.1% higher to $58.69, after industry data showed a draw in US crude stockp=
iles. Natural gas price fell 1.6% to $2.80 per 1 million BTU. Oil majors al=
so gained, with Exxon Mobil (XOM), ConocoPhillips (COP) and Chevron (CVX) a=
ll sharply higher.Among the gainers, Tyme Technologies (TYME) soared 85% af=
ter securing additional US patents for its investigational metabolomic tech=
nology platform, TYME-19, for COVID-19 treatment. Sino-Global Shipping Amer=
ica (SINO) rose 75% after naming new COO and CTO to tap Bitcoin mining. GW =
Pharma (GWPH) added 46% on acquisition by Jazz Pharma (JAZZ) for $7.2 billi=
on in a cash and stock deal.On the losing side, Vaxart (VXRT) shed 55% afte=
r its COVID-19 vaccine candidate taken by mouth showed promising results in=
 an early-stage trial but neutralizing antibodies were not detected in most=
 volunteers.In the precious metals markets, gold was up 0.2% to $1,837.80 a=
n ounce, and Silver added 2.3% to $27.02 an ounce. Copper was up 1.1% to $3=
56.40 per pound.Portfolio: Our order for CRM calls did not fill. No new rec=
ommendation today amid choppy conditions. *Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendation=
s are for monthly options expiring on the third Friday of the specified mon=
th unless otherwise noted. All stops are good after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only=
 unless otherwise specified. All orders are good for the day only unless ot=
herwise noted. "Day only" orders expire at the close of the current session=
. Past results are no guarantee of future returns. All accounts may not ach=
ieve comparable results. Recommendations are leveraged and speculative, so =
only use risk capital =E2=80=94 i.e., money you can afford to lose. All res=
ults are shown ex-commissions and fees. Options trading involves the risk o=
f substantial loss. Some news and research provided by Wall Street Journal,=
 Bloomberg, Associated Press, MT Newswires and Reuters.&nbsp;

